The Multidimensional Assessment of Interoceptive Awareness – Version 2 (MAIA-2; Mehling et al., 2018) is a 37-item adult self-report measure that assesses interoceptive awareness, or how individuals perceive, interpret, and respond to internal bodily sensations. It captures multiple dimensions of body awareness, including the ability to attend to bodily signals, regulate emotions through bodily awareness, and either engage with or avoid physical sensations. A youth version is available for use with adolescents and children (
MAIA-Y
).

